# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the ZVYRA website project following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version ^2.0.0 to dependencies
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its 25 dependencies

### 2. Code Integration (website/src/App.tsx)
- Imported `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the root level of the App component
- Placed after the Footer component to ensure it monitors all page interactions

### 3. Files Modified
- `website/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `website/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `website/src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component integration

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart):

1. **Framework**: React + Vite
2. **Package Manager**: npm
3. **Integration Point**: Root App component (website/src/App.tsx)
4. **Component Placement**: Added at the end of the JSX tree for optimal performance monitoring

The SpeedInsights component will automatically track Core Web Vitals and performance metrics once the application is deployed to Vercel. The tracking script integrates via `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` endpoints.

## Verification

✅ TypeScript type checking passes (npm run typecheck)
✅ Build completes successfully (npm run build)
✅ No linting or compilation errors
✅ Lock files properly updated

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights will automatically begin collecting performance data
2. Metrics will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section
3. Allow several days of user traffic for comprehensive analytics

## Notes

- The integration is non-intrusive and requires no additional configuration
- Performance tracking happens automatically without impacting user experience
- All changes preserve the existing code structure and functionality
